  Critical Code Generation Rules

  1. Table Name Placeholders

  - SQL uses {table_name} placeholders
  - Replace with getter calls: {batch_consumers} → tables.getBatchConsumers()
  - Use toCamelCaseCapitalized() for getter names: batch_consumers → BatchConsumers

  2. Multi-line SQL Normalization

  SQL templates may contain newlines. Always normalize:
  var normalizedSql = sql.replaceAll("\\s+", " ").trim();

  3. Generic Wildcards in JavaPoet

  // WRONG - creates "import ?;"
  ClassName.get("?", "")

  // CORRECT
  WildcardTypeName.subtypeOf(Object.class)

  4. Batch Mapper Instantiation

  // WRONG
  .map(new MapperClass())

  // CORRECT
  final var mapper = new MapperClass();
  return builder.props(data.stream().map(mapper::apply).collect(Collectors.toList()))

  5. Transaction Container Updates

  Use toBuilder() pattern, merge collections:
  // Merge messages (old + new)
  final var updatedMessages = new ArrayList<>(container.getMessages());
  updatedMessages.add(newMessage);
  return container.toBuilder()
    .messages(updatedMessages)
    .build();

  6. Lifecycle Methods

  createTable(), dropTable(), createConstraints() should NOT have @Override annotation.

  7. Transaction Save Operations

  Only include INSERT_ALL, UPDATE_ALL, DELETE_ALL (not single-entity operations):
  return switch (type) {
    case INSERT_ALL -> baseName + "Inserts";
    case UPDATE_ALL -> baseName + "Updates";
    case DELETE_ALL -> baseName + "Deletes";
    default -> null;
  };

  Use actual method names from the model, not hardcoded strings.

